course: dictionary
lesson: 8701
title: A word from America: semester
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You may hear the word semester in American films or from friends in Canada. Read the sentence around it to find its meaning. «Australia and New Zealand have four school terms a year, the UK and Ireland three, and many US schools two semesters.» The sentence compares terms with semesters, so a semester must be a part of the school year, like a term.
explain: A semester is one of the two halves of a school or college year. It is a period of learning, usually about four or five months long, with its own classes and tests. If a school has two semesters, the year is split into two halves.
explain: Some words are used in one place more than another. Semester is used mostly in the USA and Canada, and at universities everywhere. In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, schools usually say term instead.
fact: A semester is one of the two halves of a school or college year.
fact: A semester usually lasts about four or five months.
fact: «Semester» is used mostly in the USA and Canada, and at universities everywhere.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, schools usually say «term».
fact: The sentence «many US schools two semesters» shows that a year can be split into two parts.
exercise: «Many US schools have two semesters in a year.» What is a semester? | A school holiday of one week | A type of school bag | A school uniform | *One of the two halves of a school year
exercise: Ella's friend in Canada says, «My fall semester ends in December.» What does semester mean here? | *A period of learning with its own classes and tests | A type of autumn weather | A card you show at the school gate | A sports game
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Australia and New Zealand have four school terms a year» that names the same kind of school period as a semester. | Australia | year | *terms | school
test: A semester usually lasts how long? | About two years | About one week | *About four or five months | About one hour
test: Which country usually says term instead of semester? | Canada | The USA | *Australia | Universities everywhere
exam: A year at a US school has two semesters. How many semesters are there in one year? | One | Three | Four | *Two
